error[SE0434]: a `finite` state must be `bool`, `int` or a finite type
  --> tests/emit/lib/fsmbad/FsmBad.se:14:21
   |
14 |     states { finite x: double(-) = 0.0; }    // SE0434 — not finitely valued
   |                     ^ declared `double`
   = note: a finite state is the state of a state machine, which has finitely many values (§6.4)
   = help: make it `discrete` if it is a sampled value, or `continuous` if it is integrated

error[SE0433]: a `finite` state cannot be array-shaped
  --> tests/emit/lib/fsmbad/FsmBad.se:19:23
   |
19 |     states { finite x [3]: int(-) = 0; }     // SE0433 — a finite state is scalar
   |                       ^^^ an extent
   = note: a state machine's state is one value (§6.4c)
   = help: declare one `finite` state per machine

